Subject: [PATCH 1/3] =?UTF-8?q?mtp:=20--mtp-cpu-moe=20=E2=80=94=20the=20dr?=
 =?UTF-8?q?aft=20layer's=20256=20experts=20on=20the=20CPU=20(312=20MiB=20o?=
 =?UTF-8?q?f=20VRAM=20freed)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The draft layer's routed experts move to host RAM and run on the CPU, which lets an
81920-token context keep MTP drafting on a 4 GB card: the draft layer's VRAM drops
from 439 to 127 MiB. The CPU path skips CUDA graph capture and splits
capture_round/capture_step into run_round/run_step so the kernels can be launched
directly.

Measured (RTX 3050 Ti 4 GB, UD-IQ3_S): ctx 65536 decode 24.7 tok/s (87% drafts
accepted), ctx 81920 decode 18.6-21.5 tok/s (88-89%).
